0:{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[[["$","$L2","3.6",{"topic":{"id":"3.6","title":"Dark Web: Structure and Investigation Techniques","minutes":13,"summary":"Understand overlay networks and investigative boundaries without treating anonymity itself as evidence of an offence.","sections":[{"title":"Structure and legitimate uses","body":["The dark web refers to services on overlay networks that require particular software or configuration, commonly including Tor onion services. These systems can support privacy, journalism, and access under restrictive conditions as well as illicit markets. Use of anonymity technology is not, by itself, proof of criminal conduct.","Onion services use a different addressing and routing model from ordinary public websites. Hidden-service directories, introduction points, and rendezvous circuits help conceal aspects of the connection. Investigators should understand the architecture at a conceptual level; operational deanonymization is a specialized, legally constrained activity, not a classroom scanning exercise."]},{"title":"Passive collection and provenance","body":["A safe learning workflow uses supplied fictional pages or authorized passive observations. Preserve the visible content, capture time, relevant identifiers, and acquisition limitations. Do not purchase illicit goods, download unknown executables, or interact with abuse material. If such material is encountered unexpectedly, stop and follow the organization’s legal and safety procedure.","Marketplace claims, vendor names, and escrow addresses can be false or reused. Cryptocurrency transactions may provide a public ledger trail, but address ownership and transaction purpose require additional evidence. A payment graph does not automatically identify a person. Preserve the complete source and distinguish observed ledger data from inferred clustering."]},{"title":"Operational and legal limits","body":["Covert account interaction, exploitation, and network investigative techniques can affect privacy, jurisdiction, and evidential reliability. They require specific authority, careful planning, and trained personnel. A general authorization to browse public information should not be stretched into permission to deploy malware or take over a service.","Record the technical environment and any changes it makes. Routing, clock differences, and service instability can complicate timestamps. Cross-border cooperation may be needed for infrastructure records. The report should explain how the material was obtained and why the conclusion does not depend on unsupported assumptions about anonymity or location."]}],"practice":{"title":"Evaluate a supplied marketplace claim","scenario":"A fictional archived page claims that a vendor operates from a particular country.","steps":["Record the claim as page content, not verified location.","List alternative explanations such as copying, deception, or shared branding.","Identify lawful corroborating sources without contacting the vendor.","Write a confidence statement and operational safety limits."],"debrief":"The safest useful analysis often begins with source evaluation. Technical reach is not the same as legal permission or reliable attribution."},"terms":[],"lawIds":["it-act","bnss","budapest"],"sources":["budapest","nist-guide","privacy"],"unit":3,"objectives":["Explain structure and legitimate uses and apply it to an investigation.","Explain passive collection and provenance and apply it to an investigation.","Explain operational and legal limits and apply it to an investigation."],"question":{"id":"q-3.6","prompt":"What follows from a person’s use of an anonymity network?","options":["They have necessarily committed a crime.","Their identity is conclusively known.","Nothing conclusive about criminality follows without additional evidence.","All their communications are public."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Anonymity technology has lawful and unlawful uses. Conduct and statutory elements must be established separately.","unit":3}}}]],["$L3"],"$L4"]}],"isPartial":false,"staleTime":300,"varyParams":null,"buildId":"mMiCr23A_-Cpk0hZkfT7X"}
